  "question": {
    "text": "Two forces $\\bar{F}_1$ and $\\bar{F}_2$ are acting on a body. One force has magnitude thrice that of the other force and the resultant of the two forces is equal to the force of larger magnitude. The angle between $\\vec{F}_1$ and $\\vec{F}_2$ is $\\cos ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{n}\\right)$. The value of $|n|$ is _____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\left|\\vec{F}_1\\right|=\\mathrm{F} \\\\ & \\left|\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}_{\\mathrm{R}}\\right|=\\left|\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{F}}_2\\right|=3 \\mathrm{~F} \\\\ & \\mathrm{~F}_{\\mathrm{R}}^2=\\mathrm{F}_1^2+\\mathrm{F}_2^2+2 \\mathrm{~F}_1 \\mathrm{~F}_2 \\cos \\theta \\\\ & 9 \\mathrm{~F}^2=\\mathrm{F}^2+9 \\mathrm{~F}^2+6 \\mathrm{~F}^2 \\cos \\theta \\\\ & \\cos \\theta=-\\frac{1}{6} \\\\ & \\theta=\\cos ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{-6}\\right) \\\\ & \\mathrm{n}=-6 \\\\ & |\\mathrm{n}|=6\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
